    <item>
      <title>Book</title>
      <link>https://vineethchintala.com/book/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vineethchintala.com/book/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;intro-to-graph-theory&#34;&gt;Intro to Graph Theory&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I taught intro courses on graph theory at IISc (in 2024 and 2025). During this time, I was also working on my book - Graphs, Games, Algorithms. In 2020-21, I spent a year teaching Linear Algebra, Graphs and Algorithms at the University of Hyderabad.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;book-box&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#39;https://vineethchintala.com/graphs.jpg&#39; alt=&#39;Graphs, Games, Algorithms Book Cover&#39;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;book-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;h3&gt;Graphs, Games, Algorithms&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a href=&#34;https://drive.google.com/file/d/16zmmdpEycsWnPuE6XYqkX31RJ_lMnC5S/view&#34;&gt;Free eBook&lt;/a&gt;  •  &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G7Y588JN&#34;&gt;Amazon (US)&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;The book is extremely modular so read the chapters that appeal to you first. The book has four parts:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Cinema</title>
      <link>https://vineethchintala.com/movies/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vineethchintala.com/movies/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;perfect-endings-in-cinema&#34;&gt;Perfect Endings in Cinema&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Once in a while a movie elevates itself with a perfect finish, with a final unforgettable impression. It can be the difference between going home satisfied and still remembering it years later. The difference between passing joy and lifelong love.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rules:&lt;/strong&gt; In no particular order. With few words and No spoilers!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;cinema-list-container&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;script&gt;&#xA;document.addEventListener(&#34;DOMContentLoaded&#34;, function() {&#xA;    const listContainer = document.querySelector(&#39;.cinema-list-container&#39;);&#xA;    const container = listContainer.parentNode;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    let siblingBefore = listContainer.previousElementSibling;&#xA;    &#xA;    while (siblingBefore &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.tagName !== &#39;P&#39; &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.tagName !== &#39;H2&#39; &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.tagName !== &#39;BLOCKQUOTE&#39;) {&#xA;        siblingBefore = siblingBefore.previousElementSibling;&#xA;    }&#xA;    &#xA;    if (siblingBefore &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.tagName === &#39;P&#39; &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.querySelector(&#39;strong&#39;) &amp;&amp; siblingBefore.querySelector(&#39;strong&#39;).textContent.includes(&#39;Rules&#39;)) {&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.fontSize = &#39;0.82rem&#39;;&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.opacity = &#39;0.7&#39;;&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.fontFamily = &#34;-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &#39;Segoe UI&#39;, Roboto, sans-serif&#34;;&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.letterSpacing = &#39;0.02em&#39;;&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.marginTop = &#39;1.5rem&#39;;&#xA;        siblingBefore.style.marginBottom = &#39;2rem&#39;;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    const h4s = Array.from(container.querySelectorAll(&#39;h4&#39;));&#xA;&#xA;    h4s.forEach(h4 =&gt; {&#xA;        const text = h4.textContent.trim();&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        const numMatch = text.match(/^(\d+)/);&#xA;        const num = numMatch ? numMatch[1] : &#39;&#39;;&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const yearMatch = text.match(/\(?(\d{4})\)?$/);&#xA;        const year = yearMatch ? yearMatch[1] : &#39;&#39;;&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        let title = text;&#xA;        if (num) title = title.replace(/^\d+\.\s*/, &#39;&#39;);&#xA;        if (year) title = title.replace(/\s*\(?\d{4}\)?$/, &#39;&#39;).replace(/,\s*$/, &#39;&#39;);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const row = document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;        row.className = &#39;film-row&#39;;&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const titleBlock = document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;        titleBlock.className = &#39;film-title-block&#39;;&#xA;        &#xA;        const numSpan = document.createElement(&#39;span&#39;);&#xA;        numSpan.className = &#39;film-num&#39;;&#xA;        numSpan.textContent = num;&#xA;        titleBlock.appendChild(numSpan);&#xA;&#xA;        const titleText = document.createTextNode(title);&#xA;        titleBlock.appendChild(titleText);&#xA;&#xA;        if (year) {&#xA;            const yearSpan = document.createElement(&#39;span&#39;);&#xA;            yearSpan.className = &#39;film-year&#39;;&#xA;            yearSpan.textContent = ` (${year})`;&#xA;            titleBlock.appendChild(yearSpan);&#xA;        }&#xA;        &#xA;        row.appendChild(titleBlock);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const commentaryBlock = document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;        commentaryBlock.className = &#39;film-commentary&#39;;&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        let sibling = h4.nextElementSibling;&#xA;        const toMove = [];&#xA;        while (sibling &amp;&amp; sibling.tagName !== &#39;H4&#39; &amp;&amp; sibling.tagName !== &#39;SCRIPT&#39; &amp;&amp; sibling !== listContainer) {&#xA;            toMove.push(sibling);&#xA;            sibling = sibling.nextElementSibling;&#xA;        }&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        toMove.forEach(el =&gt; {&#xA;            commentaryBlock.appendChild(el);&#xA;        });&#xA;        row.appendChild(commentaryBlock);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        listContainer.appendChild(row);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        h4.parentNode.removeChild(h4);&#xA;    });&#xA;});&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;01-chungking-express-1994&#34;&gt;01. Chungking Express (1994)&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Shows how effective, and playful, symmetry can be in storytelling. After all, nothing makes a relationship look more convincing than me becoming like you and you becoming like me.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Reading</title>
      <link>https://vineethchintala.com/favourite-reads/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vineethchintala.com/favourite-reads/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;great-reading-experiences&#34;&gt;Great Reading Experiences&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Craving for a new book is like craving for a new friend - who we expect to have all the qualities of the old ones and still be able to constantly surprise us.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;reads-page-grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;reads-sidebar&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;div class=&#34;reads-menu&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &#xA;        &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;reads-content-column&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;script&gt;&#xA;document.addEventListener(&#34;DOMContentLoaded&#34;, function() {&#xA;    const pageGrid = document.querySelector(&#39;.reads-page-grid&#39;);&#xA;    const menuContainer = pageGrid.querySelector(&#39;.reads-menu&#39;);&#xA;    const contentColumn = pageGrid.querySelector(&#39;.reads-content-column&#39;);&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    const container = pageGrid.parentNode;&#xA;    const h3s = Array.from(container.querySelectorAll(&#39;h3&#39;));&#xA;    &#xA;    const sections = [];&#xA;&#xA;    h3s.forEach((h3, index) =&gt; {&#xA;        const text = h3.textContent.trim();&#xA;        const id = text.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, &#39;-&#39;);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const section = document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;        section.className = &#39;reads-section&#39;;&#xA;        section.id = id + &#39;-section&#39;;&#xA;        &#xA;        const readingContent = document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;        readingContent.className = &#39;reading-content&#39;;&#xA;        section.appendChild(readingContent);&#xA;        &#xA;        if (index === 0) {&#xA;            section.classList.add(&#39;active&#39;);&#xA;        }&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        let sibling = h3.nextElementSibling;&#xA;        const toMove = [];&#xA;        while (sibling &amp;&amp; sibling.tagName !== &#39;H3&#39; &amp;&amp; sibling.tagName !== &#39;SCRIPT&#39; &amp;&amp; sibling !== pageGrid) {&#xA;            toMove.push(sibling);&#xA;            sibling = sibling.nextElementSibling;&#xA;        }&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        toMove.forEach(el =&gt; readingContent.appendChild(el));&#xA;        &#xA;        &#xA;        contentColumn.appendChild(section);&#xA;        sections.push(section);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        const button = document.createElement(&#39;button&#39;);&#xA;        button.className = &#39;reads-menu-item&#39;;&#xA;        if (index === 0) {&#xA;            button.classList.add(&#39;active&#39;);&#xA;        }&#xA;        button.textContent = text.toUpperCase();&#xA;        button.setAttribute(&#39;data-target&#39;, id);&#xA;        &#xA;        button.addEventListener(&#39;click&#39;, function() {&#xA;            &#xA;            menuContainer.querySelectorAll(&#39;.reads-menu-item&#39;).forEach(btn =&gt; btn.classList.remove(&#39;active&#39;));&#xA;            sections.forEach(sec =&gt; sec.classList.remove(&#39;active&#39;));&#xA;&#xA;            &#xA;            this.classList.add(&#39;active&#39;);&#xA;            section.classList.add(&#39;active&#39;);&#xA;        });&#xA;&#xA;        menuContainer.appendChild(button);&#xA;&#xA;        &#xA;        h3.parentNode.removeChild(h3);&#xA;    });&#xA;});&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;fiction&#34;&gt;Fiction&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 id=&#34;in-search-of-lost-time&#34;&gt;In Search of Lost Time&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Marcel Proust&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Research</title>
      <link>https://vineethchintala.com/research/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vineethchintala.com/research/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;research&#34;&gt;Research&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The secret to doing good research is to always be a little underemployed. You waste years by not being able to waste hours - Amos Tversky&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(If you have time for only one paper, look at Two Lives.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;a-matrix-trilogy&#34;&gt;A Matrix Trilogy&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S000187082100356X?via%3Dihub&#34;&gt;Two lives: Compositions of Unimodular rows&lt;/a&gt;, Advances in Mathematics 389 (2021), 107917.    &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2101.03862.pdf&#34;&gt;[arXiv]&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;em&gt;When multiple research areas evolve around the same object, one expects that there is a connection between them. The more distinct the methods are, the more fruitful this connection will be. In this paper, we will explore this double life for unimodular rows.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://ems.press/journals/dm/articles/8965591&#34;&gt;Embeddings of Quadratic Spaces&lt;/a&gt;, Documenta Math. 23 (2018) 1621 - 1634&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://ems.press/journals/dm/articles/8965428&#34;&gt;On Suslin matrices and their connection to Spin Groups&lt;/a&gt;, Documenta Math. 20 (2015) 531 - 550.    &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.12107.pdf&#34;&gt;[arXiv]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;noncommutative-rings&#34;&gt;Noncommutative rings&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Centrality and partition of idempotents &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.08404&#34;&gt;[preprint]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A partition of finite rings makes lifting possible &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.12508&#34;&gt;[preprint]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Sorry, the nilpotents are in the center &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.11451&#34;&gt;[preprint]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/10.1142/S0219498812500892&#34;&gt;Maximum number of solutions of x&lt;sup&gt;q&lt;/sup&gt; = x in a finite noncommutative algebra&lt;/a&gt;, Journal Algebra and its applications, Volume 11, Number 5, 2012.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;microeconomics&#34;&gt;Microeconomics&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Two values are sufficient for choice consistency &lt;a href=&#34;https://osf.io/preprints/socarxiv/gf6wq/&#34;&gt;[preprint]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
